Z||000000||ElricSI||03-10-2001||03:16 PM||||This should ignite a flame war.<P>Has anyone tried or thought of trying out cars almost like the Fiero.  Like the 2nd generation MR2 which "borrowed" heavily from Fiero styling.  Maybe the Buick Reatta which was a GM 2 seater.  Honda S2000 and so on.  I looked at a new MR2 a few years ago.  It looked nice, but they wanted like 25K for it.<P>Pardon me while I put on my asbestos suit.<P>------------------<BR>Proud Owner of 85 GT||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroLisa||03-10-2001||04:33 PM||||Sure, just because I own a fiero does not mean I automatically think all other cars are crap. I love cars in general, respect most of them, just happen to own Fieros because they are cheap and easy to modify and play with. We also have a Honda S2000. It's an awesome car, fun, looks good. I also like the newest MR2s.<BR>It'd be narrow minded to not want another car only because its not a Fiero. <P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-10-2001||06:33 PM||||Personally, if I didnt find another Fiero that I wanted, and I was in the market for another car, I'd probably get a 3rd gen. Camaro, with T-Tops.  I like the styling, and there's a lot that can be done with a chevy 350.<P>Though I have never seen an MR2 in my life, if I did and it looked like it was well kept, I'd probably give the driver a smile and nod, just to acknowledge that he/she probably respects and loves their car as much as I do.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||JJ-85-2M6||03-10-2001||08:53 PM||||Since I can't get a new Fiero, my next choice would be a Miata.  I can't afford a S2000 or an Audi TT.  I have to pick something that would allow to keep my Fiero as well!  I'd miss the plastic body panels though. (I have a Saturn now) <p>[This message has been edited by JJ-85-2M6 (edited 03-10-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000004||Cooter||03-10-2001||09:08 PM||||It was my friend's Buick Reatta that turned me onto the Fiero. I like the Buick, but couldn't afford it. So I looked around for another small, GM 2 seater and found a cheap 85 SE on the back row at a cheesy car lot. I drive a Honda Civic (yes, it used to have a header and loud exhaust-but not anymore!) for my everyday transportation. I have had VW Bugs, Nissan Z cars, Camaros, S-10 trucks, and a Suburban. The Fiero is a neat car, but not the greatest. We all like them for different reasons.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||03-10-2001||09:49 PM||||Next to my Fiero GT, my last was my 2nd favorite.  A 1979 Chev Monza Spyder, 350-365hp V8 4-speed.  With some minor suspension mods, it handled almost as well a a Fiero, and better than most other (Camaros, Mustangs etc.).  It also couldn't be caught by most other cars either.<P>I don't like most of the new cars.  I think I'd have to "build my own", perhaps a kit, or get some recent vehicle that has potential to be a screamer - but then we're back to the Fiero again, aren't we  ;wink<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||danny boy||03-11-2001||04:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR> The Fiero is a neat car, but not the greatest. We all like them for different reasons.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Finally!!!  <P>I love my GT and my coupe. they are pleasing to the eye(well, not mine right now)and fun to drive, and most importantly, Different.Thats why I like them.<P><BR> I have lees $$ in BOTH my Fieros put together than I'm gonna have buying a new tranny for the Stealth!!!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||JBGehling||03-11-2001||11:31 AM||||There's many times I've considered selling my fieros and getting one of a number of things...<BR>1) A 2001 Trans-am WS6<BR>2) An older 3000 GT<BR>3) An early 90's MR2 <BR>4)a 90's twin-turbo 300ZX<P>All are sweet cars!<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||03-11-2001||07:17 PM||||I wouldn't mind driving around a later Corvair. I also would like to find a '73 Grand Am. If you're gonna mention the Reatta, you can't forget the Allante.<P>My 86 Trans Am was faster and handled better, but the T-tops made the car a worthless turd. Cuttung most of the roof off, really ruind the car. I would buy another one if a deal came along though.||||reg||1
Z||000009||danny boy||03-11-2001||07:47 PM|||| I got the privvy to ride in a 92 300ZX. It wasn't a T/T but it was still very fast and is/was the best handling car I've ever been in. Considerably slower than my Stealth but on twisty roads he has me.<BR>  Oh, one thing I forgot; '93+ Supra.If you have the $$ this is the car to have.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||03-12-2001||10:01 AM||||I like the MR2. Almost bought one in 85, until I bought my GT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>At the time, I thought the MR2 handled better, but the V-6, plastic body panels, and the INDY styling sold me. <BR>If I was going to go out and buy another completely impractical car, it would either be a Miata (Wife usta have one. Great car.) or a 3000 GT. <BR>If I buy a 4-door, it will probably be a Grand Prix, although I really want a 3.2 TL. But <I>not</I> for $30K.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
