Z||000015||LZeitgeist||03-14-2001||10:02 AM||||I'd probably go for a Miata. <P>I always loved the Cadillac Allante - the only options available were the color and whether or not you wanted the console-mounted cellphone... talk about loaded or not at all! However, I hate front-wheel-drive cars, and this was a FWDer. *sigh* (Not like I could ever afford it anyway...)<P>I've actually started appreciating the second-generation MR2's. For years, I thought they ruined the MR2 when they changed from the first generation, but now I'm liking the styling of the 2nd's much more.<P>I'd love a Ferrari 328, as long as it only cost as much to keep and maintain as a Fiero Formula, and was as easy to work on... :::chuckle:::<P>If I hadn't found my first Fiero 11 years ago, I'd probably still have my Suzuki Samurai soft-top 4x4. I miss that one. (It was the last year made before they softened the suspension to suit whiny yuppie owners, and consequently, made it easier to roll over. Stupid yuppies. It's a 5-foot long 4x4 with solid axles front and back! Of COURSE it's going to ride rough! *sigh*)<P>If I could never have another Fiero again, I'd like to find an early-to-mid 80's Firebird GTA. Those were awesome. White with t-tops and gold diamondspoke wheels and gold=plated emblems. *drool*<BR>||||reg||1
